---
import Landing from '../../layouts/Landing.astro';
import PriceTable from '../../components/PriceTable.astro';
import { pagePath } from '../../i18n';
import { q } from './faq';

const lang = 'en';
const faq = [q.access, q.fleet, q.photos, q.owns, q.sample];
---
<Landing
  lang={lang}
  page="yacht"
  title="Yacht charter video from your listing photos · Still to Film"
  description="Turn the photos on your yacht listing into a 60–90 second walkthrough video. No filming day, no crew on board, 16:9 and 9:16 included. €50 to €100 per video."
  eyebrow="For yacht charters"
  h1="Video for yacht charters, made from your listing photos"
  summary="Still to Film turns the photos already on your yacht listing into a 60–90 second walkthrough video, with no filming day and no crew on board. Videos come in 16:9 and 9:16, a person checks every one before delivery, and they cost €50 to €100 each depending on volume."
  faqTitle="Questions from charter companies"
  faqItems={faq}
  service
  related={['hotel', 'aiVideo', 'pricing']}
>
  <h2>Why is filming a charter fleet so hard?</h2>
  <p>A filming day needs the yacht in port, clean and empty, in good weather, with a crew on board for a day. In the season most yachts are out with guests, so a free day is hard to find. For a fleet, that means one shoot per yacht, spread over months.</p>
  <p>Most charter companies already have good photos of every yacht: exterior, deck, saloon, galley and cabins. Those photos are what we start from. Nothing has to be planned around the boat, and nobody needs to come on board.</p>

  <h2>How does it work?</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>You send the link</strong> to the listing, or the photos themselves.</li>
    <li><strong>We make the film.</strong> We choose the photos, the order and the camera moves, and use AI to turn the stills into calm movement.</li>
    <li><strong>A person checks it.</strong> We watch every video in full before you see it. If something does not match your photos, we fix it or cut it.</li>
    <li><strong>You give feedback.</strong> Two rounds of revisions are included.</li>
    <li><strong>You publish.</strong> You get MP4 files in 16:9 and 9:16.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>You do not need any software, prompts or an account. More detail on the <a href={pagePath(lang, 'how')}>how it works</a> page.</p>

  <h2>What do you get?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A 60 to 90 second walkthrough video per yacht.</li>
    <li>16:9 for your website and listing platforms, and 9:16 for Instagram Reels, TikTok and Stories. Both formats are included.</li>
    <li>Two rounds of revisions per video.</li>
    <li>One calm, consistent style across your whole fleet.</li>
    <li>Unlimited use for your own marketing: website, listings, social media and ads.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What can the video show, and what not?</h2>
  <p>The video can only show what is in your photos. If you have photos of the yacht underway, at anchor, on deck, in the saloon, the galley and the cabins, all of those can move. If the flybridge or a cabin was never photographed, it will not be in the film. We do not add people, views or features that are not there.</p>
  <p>The quality of the photos sets the quality of the film. Sharp, well-lit, high-resolution photos work best, and original files from your photographer work better than images saved from a website.</p>
  <p>You can see clips made from the listing photos of a motor catamaran in the <a href={pagePath(lang, 'library')}>library</a>, and compare the photo with the video on the <a href={pagePath(lang, 'home')}>home page</a>.</p>

  <h2>What does it cost?</h2>
  <p>The price per video depends on how many videos you order at once. A single video costs €100. From 5 videos it is €95 per video, and the price drops by €5 for every 5 videos, down to €50 per video.</p>
  <PriceTable lang={lang} />
  <p>For example, a fleet of 12 yachts costs 12 × €90 = €1,080, including VAT. Before you decide, we make a free sample video from your own listing photos.</p>
</Landing>
